<title>FRANCE: Air France Europe signs ground staff pay deal.</title>
<headline>Air France Europe signs ground staff pay deal.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Air France Europe, the domestic wing of the Air France group, said on Thursday it had signed a pay agreement with ground staff unions as part of a merger plan with the international airline.</p>
<p>The agreement, which was signed with the CFDT, CFTC, CGC and FO unions, means Air France Europe staff will not lose any of their benefits in the merger, the company said in a statement</p>
<p>Some Air France Europe pilots called a snap strike last Thursday, protesting against the merger plan, which would cut their salaries by around 15 percent to bring them in line with Air France counterparts.</p>
</text>
